From bb5772bffec05b8dd3ada1cb73a6c788e2ba3158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:39:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: add async_pipelines to build render pipelines in
 the background

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=async_pipelines returns from graphics pipeline
creation once the MSL exists and builds the Metal render pipeline on a
device thread pool. A draw whose pipeline is still being built waits up
to KK_ASYNC_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS (2 ms by default) and is then skipped.
Pipelines that the driver creates for its own meta operations, and
compute pipelines, are still built synchronously. Destroying a shader
waits for its build.

In Half-Life: Alyx, Metal compiling a pipeline for the first time takes up
to half a second, and pipelines created on the threads that submit work
froze the game for seconds on entering new areas.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
